#### Remedy and source scope

Under the six-Associate position, the granted termination-conspiracy summary judgment stands. The Eleventh Circuit's existing vacatur of the pendent-state-claim dismissal and common-law remand remain effective because this action began before section 1367's applicability boundary. A limitations-defense waiver is a permissible protective condition below, not a compulsory new Supreme Court instruction. Independent substantive fraud, stock, debenture, guarantee, sanctions, costs and service rulings remain at their existing scope. The two reversing Associates would remove only the categorical conspiracy ground and preserve the same independent components.

The later section 1964(c) securities-fraud restriction, criminal-conviction exception and final-conviction limitations trigger retain their terms; this termination case decides no temporal application or securities claim. No fraud, conspiracy, amount of damages or personal wrongdoing is newly found. The allegations remain the favorable summary-judgment account, not adjudicated facts.

